    "summary": "NVIDIA's board partners reportedly still lack the supply of GeForce RTX 5080 24 GB design kits, making a nearby launch seemingly impossible. These design kits typically include a GPU die and memory modules shipped directly from NVIDIA. Since this process takes time to validate and test new designs, board partners might be unable to meet the previously assumed launch in January. However, since board partners aren't receiving those GPU kits yet, this timing might be impossible to meet, and the window would be around Q1 2027, but not in January.",
